        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಬೇಟೆಯಾಡು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬೇಟೆಯಾಡು — bēṭeyāḍu — \"to hunt\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಳೆಯ ಕಾಲದಲ್ಲಿ ರಾಜರು ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಬೇಟೆಯಾಡುತ್ತಿದ್ದರು. haḷeya kāladalli rājaru kāḍinalli bēṭeyāḍuttiddaru. In the old days kings used to hunt in the forest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಬೇಟೆಯಾಡಿದೆ, bēṭeyāḍide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬೇಟೆ, a hunt, and ಆಡು, to play: to play the hunt. A hunter is a ಬೇಟೆಗಾರ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬೇಟೆಯಾಡು (bēṭeyāḍu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 5527 lists Kannada bēṭe, \"hunting, the chase\", and bēṭey āḍu, \"to hunt\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
